{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-06T12:49:29.811Z","author":"pi-glm","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"41c8bc0b9d15f82ee6cf8ca2","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-rl-upe0"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Bounded LM trainer adapter for the recursive loop"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Implement the bounded causal-LM trainer adapter for pm rl loop run: a tiny decoder-only transformer in TypeScript (1 layer, single-head causal attention, d_model<=48, Float32Array, hand-written forward/backward with a finite-difference gradient-check test over every parameter tensor), a deterministically regenerated frozen base policy pretrained on a synthetic copy task, LoRA-style low-rank adapters (rank<=4) on Q/V and the output head trained by REINFORCE with mean baseline, KL penalty to the base policy and gradient clipping, content-addressed adapter checkpoints with canonical serialization, declared fail-closed limits (max parameters, checkpoint bytes, steps, wall seconds, licences), and held-out exact-match evaluation through the existing Hoeffding promotion gate. Reuses loop.ts machinery: one gate, one promotion path."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Feature"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["execution","llm-adapter","recursive-training"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-10-06T12:49:29.811Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-06T12:49:29.811Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"pi-glm"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"A real pm CLI acceptance run of >=3 generations where gen-1 and gen-2 checkpoints differ, gen-2 collects with gen-1's promoted adapter asserted via receipts, held-out exact-match strictly improves over the base, and a contaminated run is refused; unit, property (gradient check, seed determinism), integration and performance budget tests at exact 100/100/100/100 coverage; docs/lm-adapter.md records the measured generation table"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-rl-apvf"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"29210ef65df7a4315870067ac81dfafb83ec1f6c3353b3ce6ad603770383ad65","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"ba176b04733dafc6b5d871b918c8813e33a104ccecec2c9b2c9aed59b405988c"}
